<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Recognition makes selfhood social</h2>
      <p>Self-conscious freedom is not achieved in isolation. I need another independent self to acknowledge me, and recognition must become reciprocal.</p>
      <freeform-block w="840" h="250">
        <shape preset="rightArrow" x="235" y="79" w="370" h="34" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"></shape>
        <shape preset="rightArrow" x="235" y="142" w="370" h="34" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0" flip-h="true"></shape>
        <group>
          <shape preset="ellipse" x="55" y="44" w="190" h="190" fill="surface" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="3"></shape>
          <box type="content" x="92" y="91" w="116" sizing="auto">
            <h4 align="center">Independent self</h4>
            <p role="caption" align="center">Speaks · listens · answers</p>
          </box>
        </group>
        <group>
          <shape preset="ellipse" x="595" y="44" w="190" h="190" fill="surface" stroke="palette-2" stroke-width="3"></shape>
          <box type="content" x="632" y="91" w="116" sizing="auto">
            <h4 align="center">Another independent self</h4>
            <p role="caption" align="center">Speaks · listens · answers</p>
          </box>
        </group>
        <box type="content" x="340" y="48" w="160" sizing="auto">
          <p role="caption" align="center">Acknowledges and can challenge</p>
        </box>
        <box type="content" x="340" y="183" w="160" sizing="auto">
          <p role="caption" align="center">Acknowledges and can challenge</p>
        </box>
      </freeform-block>
      <p>In the seminar, permission becomes meaningful when others listen, answer, and can challenge me in return. One-sided recognition is unstable because it denies the independence that gives recognition value.</p>
      <p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/hegel/">Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy, “Hegel”</a></p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>